A||||4||Dave85||What a differance!||||10||
Z||000000||Dave85||04-06-2000||08:13 PM||||Well, I finally got around to changing the tranny filter(auto) today and what a differance! Shifts so soooth now.  When I bought the new filter it said it should be changed every 10,000 miles.  My last one had 118,000 on it. Just a little over due!<P>Just felt like sharing.<BR>Dave||||reg||10
Z||000001||overlord||04-07-2000||12:00 AM||||tranny filter?<P>i didnt know there was a thing..i also have auto....and never changed it..let alone seen it.<P>where is it located and is it hard to change?||||reg||1
Z||000002||sully5||04-07-2000||05:54 AM||||The filter is just inside of the pan. not too difficult, just can be a little messy. Changed mine last Sunday, and if it was the original, it had 141,000 on it. I found out that the alternator bracket was busted before I had a chance to test drive it. Hope mine was as successful as yours, Dave. C yall.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dave85||04-08-2000||11:36 AM||||Sully5 is right. Not hard but messy! It only cost $10.99 for the filter and new gasket, $6.00 for tranny fluid. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||TheFiero64||04-09-2000||10:25 AM||||I would advise any fiero owner with an automatic to change the filter. When I changed my 84 SE's filter it was so hard and blocked I could hardly blow through the back of it. The car felt new again after. What a difference.||||reg||1
